From 20e10d6f482cf7119b9ae2a5a63cb602afc1fd23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:31:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: persistent vertex cache (content-addressed blocks in
 recycled arenas, adaptive bypass)

Vertex blocks whose bytes and layout were uploaded before are used in place instead of copied
again. Four 24 MiB arenas are filled in order and recycled oldest first after waiting for the
GPU; a hit costs one 64-bit hash. The cache switches itself off while fewer than 20% of the bytes
are found again. Bookkeeping is Vulkan-free and covered by tests.
